<!--
  Settings used ONLY by ops/inspect.ps1, passed with `jb inspectcode -s`. Deliberately not named
  NoofLedger.sln.DotSettings: that filename is the solution's shared layer, which Rider also reads,
  and raising these five inspections to ERROR there painted 84 findings red in the test projects -
  67 of them ClassCanBeSealed.Global against xUnit fixtures, which requirement 1 of Phase 1C exempts
  and nobody intends to fix. The severity floor exists so `-e=WARNING` reports these inspections at
  all (their default is SUGGESTION, below the floor); it is the gate's business, not the editor's.
  In Rider these stay at ReSharper's defaults, which still show them as hints where they apply.

  Dots inside an inspection id are escaped as _002E: MemberCanBePrivate.Global becomes
  MemberCanBePrivate_002EGlobal.

  InconsistentNaming is off here, and that is a decision rather than a shrug. ReSharper's default
  wants _underscore private fields; this repository does not use them, so the rule reported 25
  findings nobody would ever act on. Correcting the policy through a PredefinedNamingRules entry did
  not take effect through the CLI - tried in both the shared layer and this one, with caches cleared,
  all 25 survived - so the convention lives in .editorconfig instead, as dotnet_naming_rule entries
  the compiler enforces on every build and Rider reads too. Verified live by planting an _underscored
  field and a non-Pascal static readonly and watching IDE1006 name both.
-->
<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml" xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=InconsistentNaming/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=MemberCanBePrivate_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">ERROR</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=MemberCanBeInternal/@EntryIndexedValue">ERROR</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ClassCanBeSealed_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">ERROR</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=UnusedMember_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">ERROR</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=UnusedType_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">ERROR</s:String>
</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
